{#- Teaching, in two sections: the courses he helps teach, and the students he has mentored and tutored. It
    was one flat list of four sentences with no headings and no internal structure -- the only page on the
    site without any -- which also left a mentorship ranked level with a three-year teaching assistantship.
    Each row is laid out like a talk: the years in the gutter, the role under them as an outlined tag, the
    course and what it is about in the text column. Both lists take the ordinary step between rows: the
    Students rows carry a sentence under the title now, as the Courses rows do (deep review 2026-09-25,
    AC-12). Newest first, one direction down the whole page (FL-08). -#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block main %}

    <section id="teaching" aria-labelledby="teaching-h">
      <h1 id="teaching-h" class="inset">{{ page.heading }}</h1>
{% if page.get("intro") %}
      <p class="page-intro inset">{{ m.nb(page.intro) }}</p>
{% endif %}
    </section>

{% if site.teaching.get("courses") %}
    <section id="courses" aria-labelledby="courses-h">
      <h2 id="courses-h" class="inset">Courses</h2>
      <ul class="log log--kind" role="list">
        {{ m.teaching_rows(site.teaching.courses)|trim }}
      </ul>
    </section>
{% endif %}

{% if site.teaching.get("students") %}
    <section id="students" aria-labelledby="students-h">
      <h2 id="students-h" class="inset">Students</h2>
      <ul class="log log--kind" role="list">
        {{ m.teaching_rows(site.teaching.students)|trim }}
      </ul>
    </section>
{% endif %}

{% endblock %}
